{
  "openrpc": "1.3.2",
  "info": {
    "title": "ae/seating",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Seats for a table of people and computer players. Build the component once with createSeating(settings, identity); methods named `Seating.<name>` are members of the object it returns. Every member takes a state and returns a new one, never changing its input. Server: TypeScript `implementation/server/seating.ts` and `implementation/server/migrate.ts` (exportAll, importAll). Client lobby rows: TypeScript `implementation/web/lobby.ts`, Swift `implementation/apple/Sources/SeatRows.swift`, Kotlin `ae.seating` `SeatRows.kt` (seatRows, canTakeSeat; Swift and Kotlin take the same values as structs and enums)."
